# Read by scripts/check-noir.sh. Round circuits (bin packages under this
# directory) in round order, then the libraries whose tests it runs.
#
# The total swap is examples/amm-swap-total's round circuit
# itself, reached through the link amm_swap_total ->
# ../../amm-swap-total/circuits/amm_swap_total, not a second package here.
# That circuit already has this example's interface (the canonical prefix,
# the pool key on both sides, amount_in and direction public, the fixed
# LOAD nsk_app) and re-creates the pool note under a fresh blinding on
# ok = 0, so a copy would only be a second place to keep in step; the link
# keeps one circuit and one vk. The scripts reach it by its directory under
# circuits/ like any round here (check-noir.sh, prepare-data.sh and the e2e
# harness resolve the link); its library amm_total and its Prover cases
# live and are tested there. A round with another interface would need its
# own package on amm_total.
CIRCUITS="pss_seed amm_init amm_swap amm_swap_total"
LIBS="amm"
# The total circuits, linted by total-lint. Only amm_swap_total:
# pss_seed, amm_init and amm_swap keep their asserts (a bad amm_swap
# request is refused 422 and stores nothing), so they are not total and
# are left out.
TOTAL_CIRCUITS="amm_swap_total"
# Co-noir entries: the total circuits above call only total-noir entries whose
# hints co-noir runs (to_u64_or, add_or, mul_div_or through amm_total;
# total-noir's page "co-noir compatibility of the library's hints"), because
# the network extends their witnesses in co-noir, whose Brillig VM at the
# pinned co-snarks rev has no integer shift, mask or ConditionalMov.
# check-noir runs total-lint --brillig-ops on every circuit in CIRCUITS and
# fails on any unsupported op, but it does not run co-noir: after a change,
# also run a co-noir witness extension (the e2e, or the flow of total-noir's
# scripts/mpc-check.sh). Required inside the co-SNARK.
# No extra --lib-src (TOTAL_LIB_SRC), as in examples/amm-swap-total:
# amm_total's swap_total calls only total entries, whose hints total's src
# whitelists, and adds no hint of its own; the only reported items are std's
# (the scalar decomposition in pss_core's npk_app_hash), justified by
# pss_core's markers (scripts/check-noir.sh counts them).
